# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Research intermediates -- regenerable by-products, deliberately unversioned.
#
# None of these are inputs. They are what the scripts in research/ write out,
# and together they are ~596 MB of a ~673 MB working tree:
#
#   data/brill_traces*.jsonl      Brill harvests (--traces). 97 files, 515 MB.
#                                 Re-harvest with research/brill_remote_eval.py.
#   data/brill_dd.[0-9]*          DD tables, research/brill_dd_value.py
#   data/brill_outcomes.[0-9]*    per-board outcomes, research/brill_outcomes.py
#   data/cot_model/rejected/      superseded checkpoints the trainer kept
#   data/cot_model/*.candidate.pt an un-promoted checkpoint
#   data/cot_model/refresh_last.log*  trainer logs
#   data/examples.txt             scratch notes
#
# The canonical dataset is the layout README documents -- traces/,
# cot_dataset/, cot_model/ckpt.pt, player_models/, conventions/. Everything
# listed above sits outside it.
#
# NOTE: these files are still on disk and still in history. Ignoring them
# stops them being re-added; it does not reclaim the space in .git.
data/brill_traces*.jsonl
data/brill_dd.[0-9]*
data/brill_outcomes.[0-9]*
data/cot_model/rejected/
data/cot_model/*.candidate.pt
data/cot_model/*.candidate.pt.vocab.json
data/cot_model/refresh_last.log*
data/examples.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated trace corpora -- written by scripts, not inputs.
#
#   data/traces/corpus_combined.jsonl    refresh_student.py concatenates
#                                        traces.jsonl + disagreements.jsonl
#                                        into it
#   data/traces/disagreements.jsonl      mine_disagreements.py (Loop C)
#   data/traces/disagreements.meta.json  its stats sidecar, written by the
#                                        same run (mine_disagreements.py:244)
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `data/traces/*.jsonl`: traces.jsonl is the
# canonical corpus and the default for cot_bidder.py (CORPUS_DEFAULT),
# build_cot_dataset.py and web_export.py, and traces.meta.json is its
# provenance manifest (README: "regenerate traces when the teacher
# changes"). Both stay tracked.
data/traces/corpus_combined.jsonl
data/traces/disagreements.jsonl
data/traces/disagreements.meta.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded Brill-distillation variants.
#
# These are rungs of tuning ladders whose conclusions are recorded in
# research/status.md (§6.86-6.89) and whose recipes are written down there,
# so they are regenerable rather than inputs. Nothing loads them: not by
# path, not by stem, and not as a script default. They are also inert for
# the frozen vocabulary -- cot_tokenizer.build_frozen_vocab globs system/,
# but excludes anything matching "brill*.dsl", which covers every
# brill_distilled* file.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `system/brill_distilled_*.dsl`: the shipped
# system (brill_distilled.dsl), the leaf_ceiling default (…_control.dsl) and
# the promotion candidate (…_shipdd.dsl) must stay committable.
system/brill_distilled_578k*.dsl
system/brill_distilled_ddimp.dsl
system/brill_distilled_ddin_m*.dsl
system/brill_distilled_ddoof*.dsl
system/brill_distilled_relab_m300.dsl
system/brill_distilled_shipdd_o.dsl
